        "problem": "Simplify $\\frac{{cos}^{2}\u2061\\theta }{{csc}^{2}\u2061\\theta -1}.$",
        "worked_solution": "First, let's recall the following identity:\n\n$$\n{csc}^{2}\u2061\\theta -1={cot}^{2}\u2061\\theta \n$$\n\nSubstituting the above identity into the given expression, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{cos}^{2}\u2061\\theta }{{csc}^{2}\u2061\\theta -1} & =\\frac{{cos}^{2}\u2061\\theta }{{cot}^{2}\u2061\\theta } \\\\  & ={cos}^{2}\u2061\\theta \\cdot {tan}^{2}\u2061\\theta  \\\\  & ={cos}^{2}\u2061\\theta \\cdot \\frac{{sin}^{2}\u2061\\theta }{{cos}^{2}\u2061\\theta } \\\\  & =\\cancel{{cos}^{2}\u2061\\theta }\\cdot \\frac{{sin}^{2}\u2061\\theta }{\\cancel{{cos}^{2}\u2061\\theta }} \\\\  & ={sin}^{2}\u2061\\theta .\\end{aligned}\n$$",
